des de API y gestionar datos de manera nativa en Expo","fr":"Native-data-fetching est une compétence qui permet aux développeurs d''exécuter des requêtes API et de gérer des données de manière native dans Expo","de":"Native-data-fetching ist eine Fähigkeit, die es Entwicklern ermöglicht, API-Anfragen durchzuführen und Daten auf native Weise in Expo zu verwalten","pt":"O que é native-data-fetching? É uma habilidade para solicitações de API e fetch de dados em aplicativos móveis","ru":"Что такое native-data-fetching? Это навык для запросов API и извлечения данных в мобильных приложениях","ar":"ما هي أداة FETCH الأصلية؟ هي مهارة لطلبات API و FETCH البيانات في التطبيقات المتنقلة"},"features":{"en":["Implements API requests using expo/fetch","Sets up data fetching with React Query and SWR","Handles offline scenarios and network debugging","Implement caching strategies for optimized performance","Manages authentication and token management for secure API interactions"],"zh":["实现 API 请求","设置数据抓取（React Query、SWR）","调试网络故障","实现缓存策略","处理离线场景","身份验证/令牌管理"],"ja":["API リクエストの実装","データフェッチの設定（React Query、SWR）","ネットワーク障害のデバッグ","キャッシュ戦略の実装","オフラインシナリオの処理","認証/トークン管理"],"ko":["API 요청 구현","데이터 패칭 설정（React Query、SWR）","네트워크 오류 디버깅","캐싱 전략 구현","오프라인 시나리오 처리","인증/토큰 관리"],"es":["Soporte para solicitudes de API con expo/fetch","Depuración de errores de red y estrategias de caché","Implementación de estrategias de caché con React Query y SWR","Gestión de tokens y autenticación","Configuración de URLs de API y variables de entorno"],"fr":["Prise en charge des requêtes API avec expo/fetch","Débogage des erreurs de réseau et stratégies de cache","Mise en œuvre de stratégies de cache avec React Query et SWR","Gestion de jetons et d''authentification","Configuration des URL d''API et des variables d''environnement"],"de":["Unterstützung für API-Anfragen mit expo/fetch","Fehlersuche bei Netzwerksfehlern und Cachestrategien","Implementierung von Cachestrategien mit React Query und SWR","Verwaltung von Token und Authentifizierung","Konfiguration von API-URLs und Umgebungsvariablen"],"pt":["Implementação de solicitações de API com React Query","Configuração de fetch de dados com SWR","Depuração de falhas de rede","Implementação de estratégias de cache","Gerenciamento de autenticação e tokens"],"ru":["Реализация запросов API с React Query","Настройка извлечения данных с SWR","Отладка сети","Реализация стратегий кэширования","Управление аутентификацией и токенами"],"ar":["تنفيذ طلبات API مع React Query","تكوين FETCH البيانات مع SWR","تصحيح الأخطاء الشبكية","تنفيذ استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت","إدارة مصادقة وتوكين"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use native-data-fetching","native-data-fetching vs axios","native-data-fetching install guide","expo networking setup","react query data fetching","native-data-fetching alternative","native-data-fetching setup guide","expo fetch api requests","native-data-fetching debugging"],"zh":["Native 数据抓取","Expo Networking","API 请求","数据抓取","缓存","React Query","SWR","网络调试","AIエージェント"],"ja":["ネイティブデータフェッチング","Expo Networking","API リクエスト","データフェッチ","キャッシュ","React Query","SWR","ネットワークデバッグ","AIエージェント"],"ko":["네이티브 데이터 패칭","Expo Networking","API 요청","데이터 패칭","캐싱","React Query","SWR","네트워크 디버깅","AI 도구"],"es":["native-data-fetching","solicitudes de API","depuración de errores de red","estrategias de caché","React Query","SWR","expo/fetch","autenticación","gestión de tokens"],"fr":["native-data-fetching","requêtes API","débogage des erreurs de réseau","stratégies de cache","React Query","SWR","expo/fetch","authentification","gestion de jetons"],"de":["native-data-fetching","API-Anfragen","Netzwerksfehlerbehebung","Cachestrategien","React Query","SWR","expo/fetch","Authentifizierung","Tokenverwaltung"],"pt":["native-data-fetching","solicitações de API","fetch de dados","React Query","SWR","depuração de rede","estratégias de cache","autenticação e tokens"],"ru":["native-data-fetching","запросы API","извлечение данных","React Query","SWR","отладка сети","стратегии кэширования","аутентификация и токены"],"ar":["أداة FETCH الأصلية","طلبات API","FETCH البيانات","React Query","SWR","تصحيح الأخطاء الشبكية","استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت","مصادقة وتوكين"]}},"owner":"dannyhw","repo":"demo-design-system","repoPath":"dannyhw/demo-design-system","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-07T01:49:01.515Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"native-data-fetching","description":"Use when implementing or debugging ANY network request, API call, or data fetching. Covers fetch API, axios, React Query, SWR, error handling, caching strategies, offline support.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Expo Networking\n\n**You MUST use this skill for ANY networking work including API requests, data fetching, caching, or network debugging.**\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this router when:\n\n- Implementing API requests\n- Setting up data fetching (React Query, SWR)\n- Debugging network failures\n- Implementing caching strategies\n- Handling offline scenarios\n- Authentication/token management\n- Configuring API URLs and environment variables\n\n## Preferences\n\n- Avoid axios, prefer expo/fetch\n\n## Common Issues &","body":"# Expo Networking\n\n**You MUST use this skill for ANY networking work including API requests, data fetching, caching, or network debugging.**\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this router when:\n\n- Implementing API requests\n- Setting up data fetching (React Query, SWR)\n- Debugging network failures\n- Implementing caching strategies\n- Handling offline scenarios\n- Authentication/token management\n- Configuring API URLs and environment variables\n\n## Preferences\n\n- Avoid axios, prefer expo/fetch\n\n## Common Issues & Solutions\n\n### 1. Basic Fetch Usage\n\n**Simple GET request**:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchUser = async (userId: string) => {\n  const response = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/users/${userId}`);\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);\n  }\n\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n**POST request with body**:\n\n```tsx\nconst createUser = async (userData: UserData) => {\n  const response = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/users\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: {\n      \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n      Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,\n    },\n    body: JSON.stringify(userData),\n  });\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const error = await response.json();\n    throw new Error(error.message);\n  }\n\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. React Query (TanStack Query)\n\n**Setup**:\n\n```tsx\n// app/_layout.tsx\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      staleTime: 1000 * 60 * 5, // 5 minutes\n      retry: 2,\n    },\n  },\n});\n\nexport default function RootLayout() {\n  return (\n    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n      <Stack />\n    </QueryClientProvider>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Fetching data**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nfunction UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  const { data, isLoading, error, refetch } = useQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"user\", userId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchUser(userId),\n  });\n\n  if (isLoading) return <Loading />;\n  if (error) return <Error message={error.message} />;\n\n  return <Profile user={data} />;\n}\n```\n\n**Mutations**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useMutation, useQueryClient } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nfunction CreateUserForm() {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient();\n\n  const mutation = useMutation({\n    mutationFn: createUser,\n    onSuccess: () => {\n      // Invalidate and refetch\n      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"users\"] });\n    },\n  });\n\n  const handleSubmit = (data: UserData) => {\n    mutation.mutate(data);\n  };\n\n  return <Form onSubmit={handleSubmit} isLoading={mutation.isPending} />;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Error Handling\n\n**Comprehensive error handling**:\n\n```tsx\nclass ApiError extends Error {\n  constructor(message: string, public status: number, public code?: string) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = \"ApiError\";\n  }\n}\n\nconst fetchWithErrorHandling = async (url: string, options?: RequestInit) => {\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(url, options);\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      const error = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));\n      throw new ApiError(\n        error.message || \"Request failed\",\n        response.status,\n        error.code\n      );\n    }\n\n    return response.json();\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof ApiError) {\n      throw error;\n    }\n    // Network error (no internet, timeout, etc.)\n    throw new ApiError(\"Network error\", 0, \"NETWORK_ERROR\");\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Retry logic**:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchWithRetry = async (\n  url: string,\n  options?: RequestInit,\n  retries = 3\n) => {\n  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fetchWithErrorHandling(url, options);\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (i === retries - 1) throw error;\n      // Exponential backoff\n      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, Math.pow(2, i) * 1000));\n    }\n  }\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Authentication\n\n**Token management**:\n\n```tsx\nimport * as SecureStore from \"expo-secure-store\";\n\nconst TOKEN_KEY = \"auth_token\";\n\nexport const auth = {\n  getToken: () => SecureStore.getItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY),\n  setToken: (token: string) => SecureStore.setItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY, token),\n  removeToken: () => SecureStore.deleteItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY),\n};\n\n// Authenticated fetch wrapper\nconst authFetch = async (url: string, options: RequestInit = {}) => {\n  const token = await auth.getToken();\n\n  return fetch(url, {\n    ...options,\n    headers: {\n      ...options.headers,\n      Authorization: token ? `Bearer ${token}` : \"\",\n    },\n  });\n};\n```\n\n**Token refresh**:\n\n```tsx\nlet isRefreshing = false;\nlet refreshPromise: Promise<string> | null = null;\n\nconst getValidToken = async (): Promise<string> => {\n  const token = await auth.getToken();\n\n  if (!token || isTokenExpired(token)) {\n    if (!isRefreshing) {\n      isRefreshing = true;\n      refreshPromise = refreshToken().finally(() => {\n        isRefreshing = false;\n        refreshPromise = null;\n      });\n    }\n    return refreshPromise!;\n  }\n\n  return token;\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Offline Support\n\n**Check network status**:\n\n```tsx\nimport NetInfo from \"@react-native-community/netinfo\";\n\n// Hook for network status\nfunction useNetworkStatus() {\n  const [isOnline, setIsOnline] = useState(true);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    return NetInfo.addEventListener((state) => {\n      setIsOnline(state.isConnected ?? true);\n    });\n  }, []);\n\n  return isOnline;\n}\n```\n\n**Offline-first with React Query**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { onlineManager } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\nimport NetInfo from \"@react-native-community/netinfo\";\n\n// Sync React Query with network status\nonlineManager.setEventListener((setOnline) => {\n  return NetInfo.addEventListener((state) => {\n    setOnline(state.isConnected ?? true);\n  });\n});\n\n// Queries will pause when offline and resume when online\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Environment Variables\n\n**Using environment variables for API configuration**:\n\nExpo supports environment variables with the `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix. These are inlined at build time and available in your JavaScript code.\n\n```tsx\n// .env\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_VERSION=v1\n\n// Usage in code\nconst API_URL = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL;\n\nconst fetchUsers = async () => {\n  const response = await fetch(`${API_URL}/users`);\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n**Environment-specific configuration**:\n\n```tsx\n// .env.development\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000\n\n// .env.production\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.production.com\n```\n\n**Creating an API client with environment config**:\n\n```tsx\n// api/client.ts\nconst BASE_URL = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL;\n\nif (!BASE_URL) {\n  throw new Error(\"EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is not defined\");\n}\n\nexport const apiClient = {\n  get: async <T,>(path: string): Promise<T> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}${path}`);\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n\n  post: async <T,>(path: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}${path}`, {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n      body: JSON.stringify(body),\n    });\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n};\n```\n\n**Important notes**:\n\n- Only variables prefixed with `EXPO_PUBLIC_` are exposed to the client bundle\n- Never put secrets (API keys with write access, database passwords) in `EXPO_PUBLIC_` variables—they''re visible in the built app\n- Environment variables are inlined at **build time**, not runtime\n- Restart the dev server after changing `.env` files\n- For server-side secrets in API routes, use variables without the `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix\n\n**TypeScript support**:\n\n```tsx\n// types/env.d.ts\ndeclare global {\n  namespace NodeJS {\n    interface ProcessEnv {\n      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL: string;\n      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_VERSION?: string;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport {};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Request Cancellation\n\n**Cancel on unmount**:\n\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const controller = new AbortController();\n\n  fetch(url, { signal: controller.signal })\n    .then((response) => response.json())\n    .then(setData)\n    .catch((error) => {\n      if (error.name !== \"AbortError\") {\n        setError(error);\n      }\n    });\n\n  return () => controller.abort();\n}, [url]);\n```\n\n**With React Query** (automatic):\n\n```tsx\n// React Query automatically cancels requests when queries are invalidated\n// or components unmount\n```\n\n---\n\n## Decision Tree\n\n```\nUser asks about networking\n  |-- Basic fetch?\n  |   \\-- Use fetch API with error handling\n  |\n  |-- Need caching/state management?\n  |   |-- Complex app -> React Query (TanStack Query)\n  |   \\-- Simpler needs -> SWR or custom hooks\n  |\n  |-- Authentication?\n  |   |-- Token storage -> expo-secure-store\n  |   \\-- Token refresh -> Implement refresh flow\n  |\n  |-- Error handling?\n  |   |-- Network errors -> Check connectivity first\n  |   |-- HTTP errors -> Parse response, throw typed errors\n  |   \\-- Retries -> Exponential backoff\n  |\n  |-- Offline support?\n  |   |-- Check status -> NetInfo\n  |   \\-- Queue requests -> React Query persistence\n  |\n  |-- Environment/API config?\n  |   |-- Client-side URLs -> EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix in .env\n  |   |-- Server secrets -> Non-prefixed env vars (API routes only)\n  |   \\-- Multiple environments -> .env.development, .env.production\n  |\n  \\-- Performance?\n      |-- Caching -> React Query with staleTime\n      |-- Deduplication -> React Query handles this\n      \\-- Cancellation -> AbortController or React Query\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n**Wrong: No error handling**\n\n```tsx\nconst data = await fetch(url).then((r) => r.json());\n```\n\n**Right: Check response status**\n\n```tsx\nconst response = await fetch(url);\nif (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\nconst data = await response.json();\n```\n\n**Wrong: Storing tokens in AsyncStorage**\n\n```tsx\nawait AsyncStorage.setItem(\"token\", token); // Not secure!\n```\n\n**Right: Use SecureStore for sensitive data**\n\n```tsx\nawait SecureStore.setItemAsync(\"token\", token);\n```\n\n## Example Invocations\n\nUser: \"How do I make API calls in React Native?\"\n-> Use fetch, wrap with error handling\n\nUser: \"Should I use React Query or SWR?\"\n-> React Query for complex apps, SWR for simpler needs\n\nUser: \"My app needs to work offline\"\n-> Use NetInfo for status, React Query persistence for caching\n\nUser: \"How do I handle authentication tokens?\"\n-> Store in expo-secure-store, implement refresh flow\n\nUser: \"API calls are slow\"\n-> Check caching strategy, use React Query staleTime\n\nUser: \"How do I configure different API URLs for dev and prod?\"\n-> Use EXPO*PUBLIC* env vars with .env.development and .env.production files\n\nUser: \"Where should I put my API key?\"\n-> Client-safe keys: EXPO*PUBLIC* in .env. Secret keys: non-prefixed env vars in API routes only\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-07T01:59:47.037Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing seamless Expo networking and data fetching capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要无缝 Expo 网络和数据获取能力的全栈代理。","ja":"Expo ネットワーキングとデータ取得機能をシームレスに必要とするフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"無결점의 Expo 네트워킹과 데이터 가져오기 능력이 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Full Stack que necesitan funcionalidades de networking y fetching de datos de Expo sin problemas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack ayant besoin de fonctionnalités de mise en réseau et de récupération de données Expo sans interruption.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die eine nahtlose Expo-Netzwerkinfrastruktur und Datenabrufmöglichkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que necessitam de recursos de rede e capacidades de busca de dados Expo sem interrupções.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Full Stack, которым необходимы бесперебойные возможности сети Expo и извлечения данных.","ar":"مثالي لعميل كامل النطاق الذي يحتاج إلى شبكة Expo وخاصية استرجاع البيانات دون انقطاع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to handle Expo networking tasks, including API requests, data fetching, and caching, using React Query, SWR, and Expo, while preferring expo/fetch over axios for optimized performance.","zh":"赋予代理处理 Expo 网络任务的能力，包括使用 React Query、SWR 和 Expo 的 API 请求、数据获取和缓存，而优先使用 expo/fetch 而不是 axios 以获得优化的性能。","ja":"エージェントが Expo ネットワーキング タスクを処理できるようにし、React Query、SWR、Expo を使用した API リクエスト、データ取得、キャッシングを行い、パフォーマンスを最適化するために axios よりも expo/fetch を優先します。","ko":"에이전트가 Expo 네트워킹 작업을 처리할 수 있도록 하며, React Query, SWR, Expo를 사용한 API 요청, 데이터 가져오기, 캐싱을 수행하며, 성능을 최적화하기 위해 axios보다 expo/fetch를 선호합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a manejar tareas de networking de Expo, incluyendo solicitudes de API, recuperación de datos y almacenamiento en caché, utilizando React Query, SWR y Expo, mientras prefiere expo/fetch sobre axios para un rendimiento optimizado.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les tâches de mise en réseau Expo, notamment les requêtes API, la récupération de données et la mise en cache, en utilisant React Query, SWR et Expo, tout en préférant expo/fetch à axios pour des performances optimisées.","de":"Ermöglich es Agents, Expo-Netzwerkaufgaben zu verwalten, einschließlich API-Anfragen, Datenabruf und Caching, unter Verwendung von React Query, SWR und Expo, während expo/fetch gegenüber axios für optimierte Leistung bevorzugt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a lidar com tarefas de rede Expo, incluindo solicitações de API, busca de dados e cache, usando React Query, SWR e Expo, preferindo expo/fetch em vez de axios para desempenho otimizado.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять задачи сети Expo, включая запросы API, извлечение данных и кэширование, используя React Query, SWR и Expo, отдавая предпочтение expo/fetch вместо axios для оптимизированной производительности.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التعامل مع مهام شبكة Expo، بما في ذلك طلبات API واسترجاع البيانات وذاكرة التخزين المؤقت، باستخدام React Query وSWR وExpo، مع تفضيل expo/fetch على axios لأداء محسّن."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing API requests with expo/fetch","Setting up data fetching with React Query and SWR","Debugging network failures and implementing caching strategies"],"zh":["使用 expo/fetch 实现 API 请求","使用 React Query 和 SWR 设置数据获取","调试网络故障并实现缓存策略"],"ja":["expo/fetch を使用して API リクエストを実装する","React Query と SWR を使用してデータ取得を設定する","ネットワーク障害をデバッグし、キャッシング戦略を実装する"],"ko":["expo/fetch를 사용하여 API 요청을 구현하는 것","React Query와 SWR를 사용하여 데이터 가져오기를 설정하는 것","네트워크 오류를 디버깅하고 캐싱 전략을 구현하는 것"],"es":["Implementar solicitudes de API con expo/fetch","Configurar la recuperación de datos con React Query y SWR","Depurar fallos de red y implementar estrategias de caché"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des requêtes API avec expo/fetch","Configurer la récupération de données avec React Query et SWR","Déboguer les défaillances du réseau et mettre en œuvre des stratégies de mise en cache"],"de":["Implementieren von API-Anfragen mit expo/fetch","Einrichten des Datenabrufs mit React Query und SWR","Fehler bei Netzwerkverbindungen debuggen und Caching-Strategien implementieren"],"pt":["Implementar solicitações de API com expo/fetch","Configurar busca de dados com React Query e SWR","Depurar falhas de rede e implementar estratégias de cache"],"ru":["Реализация запросов API с помощью expo/fetch","Настройка извлечения данных с помощью React Query и SWR","Отладка сбоев сети и реализация стратегий кэширования"],"ar":["تنفيذ طلبات API مع expo/fetch","تكوين استرجاع البيانات مع React Query وSWR","تصحيح أعطال الشبكة وتنفيذ استراتيجيات الذاكرة المؤقتة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Expo environment","Prefer expo/fetch over axios for networking tasks"],"zh":["需要 Expo 环境","优先使用 expo/fetch 而不是 axios 进行网络任务"],"ja":["Expo 環境が必要","ネットワーク タスクには axios よりも expo/fetch を優先する"],"ko":["Expo 환경이 필요함","네트워킹 작업에 대해 axios보다 expo/fetch를 선호함"],"es":["Requiere entorno Expo","Preferir expo/fetch sobre axios para tareas de networking"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Expo","Préférer expo/fetch à axios pour les tâches de mise en réseau"],"de":["Erfordert Expo-Umgebung","Bevorzugen von expo/fetch gegenüber axios für Netzwerkaufgaben"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Expo","Preferir expo/fetch em vez de axios para tarefas de rede"],"ru":["Требуется окружение Expo","Предпочтение expo/fetch вместо axios для задач сети"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Expo","الترجيح لاستخدام expo/fetch بدلاً من axios لمهام الشبكة"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"b4e72ed9215cac46f40a461e816acd634797512d97e39477925087eccc6220be","qualityScore":53}');
