pr es una herramienta de código abierto que analiza solicitudes de extracción y carga datos utilizando Python","fr":"Review-pr est un outil open source qui analyse les demandes d''extraction et charge des données en utilisant Python","de":"Review-pr ist ein Open-Source-Tool, das Pull-Anfragen analysiert und Daten mit Python lädt","pt":"O que é Review-PR? É uma ferramenta de análise de pull requests em Python que facilita a revisão e análise de código","ru":"Что такое ИИ Агент Review-PR? Это инструмент для анализа пулл-реквестов на Python, который упрощает процесс ревью и анализа кода","ar":"ما هي أداة Review-PR؟ هي أداة لتحليل الطلبات السحابية باستخدام Python التي تسهل عملية المراجعة والتحليل الشامل للكود"},"features":{"en":["Parses $ARGUMENTS to extract PR identifiers and reviewer instructions","Analyzes pull requests using the extracted PR identifier (PR_ID)","Supports optional reviewer instructions for additional context","Gathers data in paragraphs for streamlined review","Utilizes Python for efficient data loading and analysis"],"zh":["支持数据加载和分析","集成 ELT 和数据仓库","使用 Python 进行开发","支持数据湖和数据仓库","提供数据加载和分析工具"],"ja":["データローディングと分析をサポート","ELT とデータウェアハウス統合","Python を使用した開発","データレイクとデータウェアハウスのサポート","データローディングと分析ツールの提供"],"ko":["데이터 로딩과 분석을 지원","ELT와 데이터 웨어하우스 통합","Python을 사용한 개발","데이터 레이크와 데이터 웨어하우스 지원","데이터 로딩과 분석 도구 제공"],"es":["Análisis de solicitudes de extracción con PR_ID","Carga de datos utilizando la biblioteca Python DLT","Soporte para instrucciones de revisión adicionales","Extracción de datos de manera eficiente","Carga de datos en un lago de datos o almacén de datos","Integración con herramientas de ingeniería de datos como ELT"],"fr":["Analyse des demandes d''extraction avec PR_ID","Chargement de données en utilisant la bibliothèque Python DLT","Prise en charge d''instructions de révision supplémentaires","Extraction de données de manière efficace","Chargement de données dans un lac de données ou un entrepôt de données","Intégration avec des outils d''ingénierie de données tels que ELT"],"de":["Analyse von Pull-Anfragen mit PR_ID","Datenladen mit der Python-Bibliothek DLT","Unterstützung für zusätzliche Überprüfungsanweisungen","Effizientes Extrahieren von Daten","Datenladen in ein Datenlager oder Data-Warehouse","Integration mit DatenEngineering-Tools wie ELT"],"pt":["Análise de pull requests em Python","Extração do identificador da PR e instruções do revisor","Suporte a linha de comando para personalização","Integração com fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento","Melhoria da eficiência do processo de revisão","Suporte a dados de carga e análise de código"],"ru":["Анализ пулл-реквестов на Python","Извлечение идентификатора пулл-реквеста и инструкций ревьюера","Поддержка командной строки для настройки","Интеграция с рабочими процессами разработки","Повышение эффективности процесса ревью","Поддержка данных загрузки и анализа кода"],"ar":["تحليل الطلبات السحابية باستخدام Python","استخراج معرّف الطلب السحابي وتعليمات المراجع","دعم سطر الأوامر للتعديل","التكامل مع تدفقات عمل التطوير","تحسين كفاءة عملية المراجعة","دعم بيانات التحميل والتحليل الشامل للكود"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use review-pr","review-pr alternative","review-pr setup guide","what is review-pr","review-pr vs github","review-pr install","review-pr for data engineers","review-pr for python developers","review-pr data loading","review-pr pull request analysis"],"zh":["review-pr","Python 数据加载","ELT","数据仓库","数据湖","数据分析","AI 代理","数据加载工具"],"ja":["review-pr","Python データローディング","ELT","データウェアハウス","データレイク","データ分析","AI エージェント","データローディングツール"],"ko":["review-pr","Python 데이터 로딩","ELT","데이터 웨어하우스","데이터 레이크","데이터 분석","AI 에이전트","데이터 로딩 도구"],"es":["review-pr","carga de datos","análisis de solicitudes de extracción","DLT","Python","ingeniería de datos","lago de datos","almacén de datos","ELT","herramientas de AI"],"fr":["review-pr","chargement de données","analyse des demandes d''extraction","DLT","Python","ingénierie de données","lac de données","entrepôt de données","ELT","outils d''IA"],"de":["review-pr","Datenladen","Analyse von Pull-Anfragen","DLT","Python","Datenengineering","Datenlager","Data-Warehouse","ELT","KI-Tools"],"pt":["review-pr","análise de pull requests","python","desenvolvimento de software","fluxo de trabalho","eficiência","análise de código","dados de carga","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["review-pr","анализ пулл-реквестов","python","разработка программного обеспечения","рабочий процесс","эффективность","анализ кода","данные загрузки","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["review-pr","تحليل الطلبات السحابية","python","تطوير البرمجيات","تدفق عمل","كفاءة","تحليل الكود","بيانات التحميل","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"dlt-hub","repo":"dlt","repoPath":"dlt-hub/dlt","stars":4949,"forks":458,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T16:53:33Z","topics":["data","data-engineering","data-lake","data-loading","data-warehouse","elt","extract","load","python","transform"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"review-pr","description":"Analyze a GitHub pull request including diff, comments, related issues, and local code context","bodyPreview":"# Review Pull Request\n\nParse `$ARGUMENTS` to extract the PR identifier and optional reviewer instructions:\n- Everything before the first `--` (or all of it, if there is no `--`) is the **PR identifier** (URL or number). Referred to as `PR_ID` below.\n- Everything after the first `--` is **reviewer instructions** — additional focus areas or context from the caller. If absent, there are no special instructions.\n\nAnalyze the pull request: PR_ID\n\n## Steps\n\nRun the following steps. Gather data in para","body":"# Review Pull Request\n\nParse `$ARGUMENTS` to extract the PR identifier and optional reviewer instructions:\n- Everything before the first `--` (or all of it, if there is no `--`) is the **PR identifier** (URL or number). Referred to as `PR_ID` below.\n- Everything after the first `--` is **reviewer instructions** — additional focus areas or context from the caller. If absent, there are no special instructions.\n\nAnalyze the pull request: PR_ID\n\n## Steps\n\nRun the following steps. Gather data in parallel where possible.\n\n### 1. Set up worktree\n\nResolve the PR number:\n\n```\ngh pr view PR_ID --json number\n```\n\nUse the number to form the worktree name `review-pr-<number>`.\n\nInvoke the `/create-worktree review-pr-<number> --pr <number>` skill to create an isolated worktree for this PR. Note the worktree path from the skill output — referred to as `WORKTREE` below.\n\nVerify that the cwd is now inside the worktree:\n\n```\npwd\n```\n\nIf `pwd` does not show `WORKTREE`, run `cd WORKTREE` and verify again. Stop with an error if the cwd cannot be set. Once confirmed, subsequent Bash calls will run inside the worktree automatically.\n\n### 2. Fetch PR metadata and diff\n\nUse `gh` to collect all PR information in parallel:\n\n- `gh pr view PR_ID --json title,body,author,state,baseRefName,headRefName,number,url,comments,reviews,labels,milestone`\n- `gh pr diff PR_ID`\n\n### 3. Check dependency changes in `pyproject.toml`\n\nIf the PR diff (from step 2) touches `pyproject.toml`, run the automated dependency checker.\n\nFirst, fetch the latest `devel` from origin so the comparison is against the current state:\n\n```\ngit fetch origin devel\n```\n\nThen run the script — always compare against `origin/devel` regardless of the PR''s base branch:\n\n```\npython tools/check_dependency_changes.py origin/devel\n```\n\nThe script finds the merge-base, simulates a three-way merge (like GitHub), and reports:\n- **Main dependencies** (`[project.dependencies]`) — displayed as WARNING (these affect every user)\n- **Optional dependencies** (`[project.optional-dependencies]`) — displayed as WARNING (these affect users of specific extras)\n- **Dev/group dependencies** (`[dependency-groups]`) — listed for awareness (no impact on end users)\n- **Merge conflicts** — if `pyproject.toml` would conflict, the script warns and falls back to showing the PR''s intended changes\n\nInclude the script output verbatim in the review. If the script exits with code 1 (changes detected), flag dependency changes in the review verdict. If it exits with code 2 (conflicts), flag that `pyproject.toml` needs conflict resolution.\n\nIf `pyproject.toml` is not in the diff, skip this step.\n\n### 4. Check CI lint and mypy status\n\nUse `gh pr checks PR_ID` to retrieve the CI check results. Look for checks matching `lint on all python versions / lint*` — these run mypy, ruff, flake8, bandit, and docstring checks across Python 3.9–3.13 (defined in `.github/workflows/lint.yml`).\n\n- Report the status of each lint check (pass/fail/pending).\n- If any lint check has failed, fetch its logs with `gh run view <run-id> --log-failed` to identify the specific errors (mypy type errors, ruff violations, etc.).\n- Include lint/mypy status in the final review verdict. A failing lint check should be flagged as a required fix.\n\n### 5. Analyze related issues\n\nExtract any issue references from the PR body (e.g. `fixes #1234`, `closes #1234`, `#1234`). For each referenced issue, fetch it with:\n\n- `gh issue view <number> --json title,body,author,state,comments,labels`\n\nUnderstand the original problem being solved.\n\n### 6. Analyze the code\n\nUsing absolute paths under `WORKTREE`:\n\n- Read the changed files in full to understand context beyond the diff.\n- Look at callers/callees of modified functions.\n- Check if similar patterns exist elsewhere that should also be updated.\n- Review the coding style and code patterns to conform with @CLAUDE.md\n- If **reviewer instructions** were provided, pay special attention to the areas or concerns they describe during this analysis.\n- Mention only crucial finding to the user in the initial overview. Avoid code snippets except if critical bugs were found\n\n### 7. Review test coverage\n\n#### 7a. Define the testing scope\n\nBased on the PR changes, identify what needs to be tested:\n\n- What are the distinct behaviors introduced or modified?\n- What are the edge cases and error paths?\n- What are the integration boundaries (e.g., does the change affect how components interact)?\n\nProduce a checklist of required test scenarios before evaluating existing tests.\n\n#### 7b. Evaluate existing tests against the checklist\n\n- Compare the PR''s tests against the required scenarios checklist. Flag any gaps.\n- Flag any tests that verify things outside the PR''s scope or test obvious/trivial behavior that adds no value.\n\n#### 7c. Verify tests are in the right modules\n\n- Search the test directory for where similar functionality is already tested (grep for related function names, class names, or feature keywords).\n- New tests should live alongside related existing tests, not in new files unless the PR introduces an entirely new module.\n- Flag tests placed in the wrong location.\n\n#### 7d. Check for duplication and over-testing\n\n- Look for tests that cover nearly identical cases and could be merged or parametrized with `@pytest.mark.parametrize`.\n- Look for repeated setup/assertion logic across tests that should be extracted into a helper or fixture.\n- If multiple tests differ only in a single variable (e.g., `True`/`False`, different type values), they must be parametrized into one test function.\n- Flag any copy-paste test code. Minimizing test code maintenance burden is a priority.\n\n#### 7e. Bug Fixes Should Have Regression Tests\nIf the PR fixes a bug:\n- Is there a test that would have caught the bug before the fix?\n- Does the test verify the specific scenario from the bug report?\n\n### 8. Check documentation coverage\n\nIf the PR modifies public API (new parameters, changed behavior, new configuration options, new functions/classes exposed to users):\n\n- Search `WORKTREE/docs/website/docs/` for existing documentation covering the topic of the PR.\n- If the topic is already documented and the PR changes its behavior or adds new options, verify that the PR also updates the relevant doc pages.\n- If documentation updates are missing, flag this in the review as a required change.\n- If the topic is not documented at all, this is not a blocker — don''t require docs for previously undocumented internals.\n\n### 9. Produce the review\n\nWrite a structured analysis covering:\n\n- **Summary**: What the PR does and why, referencing the linked issue.\n- **Changes**: Breakdown of changes should be concise, avoid code samples\n- **Dependency Changes**: If `pyproject.toml` was modified, include the warnings and listings from step 3. Main and optional dependency changes must appear as yellow WARNING blocks. Omit this section if no dependency changes were found.\n- **CI Lint & Mypy**: Status of lint checks across Python versions. If any failed, list the specific errors.\n- **Observations & Potential Issues**: Bugs, edge cases, missing error handling, performance concerns, memory issues, security issues, backward compatibility.\n- **Breaking Changes and Public API**: Follow the rules on breaking changes and Public API and report issues.\n- **Test Coverage**: Required scenarios checklist with pass/fail status, misplaced tests, duplication issues, parametrization opportunities.\n- **Documentation**: Whether doc updates are needed and if they were provided.\n- **Reviewer Instructions**: If reviewer instructions were provided, include a dedicated section addressing each point raised. If no instructions were provided, omit this section.\n- **Verdict**: Overall assessment.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-06T06:25:10.864Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing comprehensive pull request analysis and review capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要全面拉取请求分析和审查功能的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが包括的なプルリクエスト分析およびレビュー機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 포괄적인 풀 요청 분석 및 리뷰 기능을 필요로 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan un análisis y capacidad de revisión de solicitudes de extracción comprehensivos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une analyse et de capacités de révision de demande d''extraction complètes.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine umfassende Analyse und Überprüfungsfunktionen für Pull-Requests benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de análise e revisão abrangentes de solicitações de pull.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходимы всесторонние анализ и обзор запросов на слияние.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات开发 التي تحتاج إلى تحليل واستعراض شامليين لطلبات السحب."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to parse PR identifiers and reviewer instructions, providing advanced pull request analysis using $ARGUMENTS and PR_ID, with optional reviewer context for data engineers and developers.","zh":"使代理能够解析 PR 标识符和审查者指令，使用 $ARGUMENTS 和 PR_ID 提供高级拉取请求分析，并为数据工程师和开发人员提供可选的审查者上下文。","ja":"エージェントが PR 識別子とレビューアの指示を解析し、$ARGUMENTS と PR_ID を使用して高度なプルリクエスト分析を提供し、データエンジニアと開発者向けにオプションのレビューアコンテキストを提供することを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 PR 식별자와 리뷰어 지침을 구문 분석하여 $ARGUMENTS 및 PR_ID를 사용하여 고급 풀 요청 분석을 제공하고 데이터 엔지니어 및 개발자에게 선택적 리뷰어 컨텍스트를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a analizar identificadores de PR y instrucciones del revisor, proporcionando un análisis avanzado de solicitudes de extracción utilizando $ARGUMENTS y PR_ID, con contexto de revisor opcional para ingenieros de datos y desarrolladores.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''analyser les identificateurs de PR et les instructions du réviseur, fournissant une analyse avancée de demande d''extraction en utilisant $ARGUMENTS et PR_ID, avec un contexte de réviseur facultatif pour les ingénieurs de données et les développeurs.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, PR-Identifikatoren und Revisoranweisungen zu parsen und erweiterte Pull-Request-Analysen unter Verwendung von $ARGUMENTS und PR_ID bereitzustellen, mit optionalen Revisor-Kontext für Daten-Engineers und Entwickler.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a analisar identificadores de solicitações de pull e instruções de revisores, fornecendo análise avançada de solicitações de pull usando $ARGUMENTS e PR_ID, com contexto opcional de revisor para engenheiros de dados e desenvolvedores.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью анализировать идентификаторы запросов на слияние и инструкции рецензентов, обеспечивая расширенный анализ запросов на слияние с использованием $ARGUMENTS и PR_ID, с опциональным контекстом рецензента для инженеров данных и разработчиков.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحليل معرفات طلبات السحب وتعليمات المراجعين، وتوفير تحليل متقدم لطلبات السحب باستخدام $ARGUMENTS و PR_ID، مع سياق مرجعي اختياري لمهندسي البيانات والمطورين."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing pull requests for code quality","Extracting reviewer instructions for focused feedback","Automating PR review workflows with customized instructions"],"zh":["分析拉取请求的代码质量","提取审查者指令以获得集中反馈","使用自定义指令自动化 PR 审查工作流"],"ja":["コード品質のプルリクエストを分析する","集中フィードバックのためにレビューアの指示を抽出する","カスタマイズされた指示で PR レビュー ワークフローを自動化する"],"ko":["코드 품질의 풀 요청 분석","집중 피드백을 위해 리뷰어 지침 추출","사용자 지정 지침으로 PR 리뷰 워크플ロー 자동화"],"es":["Análisis de solicitudes de extracción para la calidad del código","Extracción de instrucciones del revisor para comentarios enfocados","Automatización de flujos de trabajo de revisión de PR con instrucciones personalizadas"],"fr":["Analyse de demandes d''extraction pour la qualité du code","Extraction des instructions du réviseur pour des commentaires ciblés","Automatisation des flux de travail de révision de PR avec des instructions personnalisées"],"de":["Analyse von Pull-Requests für die Code-Qualität","Extraktion von Revisoranweisungen für fokussierte Feedback","Automatisierung von PR-Überprüfungs-Workflows mit angepassten Anweisungen"],"pt":["Analisar solicitações de pull para qualidade de código","Extrair instruções de revisores para comentários focados","Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de revisão de solicitações de pull com instruções personalizadas"],"ru":["Анализ запросов на слияние для качества кода","Извлечение инструкций рецензентов для целенаправленных отзывов","Автоматизация рабочих процессов обзора запросов на слияние с индивидуальными инструкциями"],"ar":["تحليل طلبات السحب لجودة الشفرة","استخراج تعليمات المراجعين لتعليقات مركزة","تحسين سير عمل استعراض طلبات السحب بإرشادات مخصصة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires $ARGUMENTS parsing","Limited to pull request analysis"],"zh":["需要 $ARGUMENTS 解析","仅限拉取请求分析"],"ja":["$ARGUMENTS パースが必要","プルリクエスト分析のみ"],"ko":["$ARGUMENTS 구문 분석 필요","풀 요청 분석 전용"],"es":["Requiere análisis de $ARGUMENTS","Limitado al análisis de solicitudes de extracción"],"fr":["Nécessite l''analyse de $ARGUMENTS","Limité à l''analyse de demande d''extraction"],"de":["Erfordert $ARGUMENTS-Parsing","Begrenzt auf Pull-Request-Analyse"],"pt":["Requer análise de $ARGUMENTS","Limitado à análise de solicitações de pull"],"ru":["Требует анализа $ARGUMENTS","Ограничен анализом запросов на слияние"],"ar":["يتطلب تحليل $ARGUMENTS","محدود بتحليل طلبات السحب"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"4840da2d82e0aaad3006247d17cd0b78c8634e1a4a6d6fa9f3d11927c219260d","qualityScore":52}');
