使用Rust编写，目标是提高代码质量和性能","ja":"fix-repoはRuboCopの実験的なリライトであり、Rustで書かれており、コード品質とパフォーマンスを向上させることを目的としています","ko":"fix-repo는 루비코프의 실험적인 재구현으로, 러스트로 작성되어 코드 품질과 성능을 향상시키는 것을 목표로 합니다","es":"Fix-repo es una versión experimental de RuboCop reescrita en Rust, diseñada para mejorar la eficiencia y el rendimiento","fr":"Fix-repo est une version expérimentale de RuboCop réécrite en Rust, conçue pour améliorer l''efficacité et les performances","de":"Fix-repo ist eine experimentelle Version von RuboCop, die in Rust neu geschrieben wurde, um die Effizienz und Leistung zu verbessern","pt":"O Fix-Repo é uma reescrita experimental do RuboCop em Rust, visando melhorar a performance e a produtividade do desenvolvedor Ruby","ru":"Fix-Repo - это экспериментальная переписка RuboCop на Rust, направленная на улучшение производительности и продуктивности разработчика Ruby","ar":"أداة إصلاح المستودع هي إعادة كتابة تجريبية لروبوكوب في روست، تهدف إلى تحسين الأداء وإنتاجية مطور روبي","en":"Experimental RuboCop rewrite in Rust"},"definition":{"en":"Experimental RuboCop rewrite in Rust"},"features":{"zh":["基于Rust的高性能实现","实验性的RuboCop重写","提高代码质量和性能","支持Ruby代码的静态分析","易于集成到现有项目中"],"ja":["Rustで書かれた高パフォーマンスな実装","RuboCopの実験的なリライト","コード品質とパフォーマンスの向上","Rubyコードの静的解析をサポート","既存のプロジェクトへの容易な統合"],"ko":["러스트로 구현된 고성능 기능","루비코프의 실험적인 재구현","코드 품질과 성능의 향상","루비 코드의 정적 분석을 지원","既存 프로젝트への 쉽게 통합"],"es":["Reescritura de RuboCop en Rust","Mejora de la eficiencia y el rendimiento","Código abierto y personalizable","Compatibilidad con Ruby y Rust","Análisis de código y corrección de errores"],"fr":["Réécriture de RuboCop en Rust","Amélioration de l''efficacité et des performances","Code open source et personnalisable","Compatibilité avec Ruby et Rust","Analyse de code et correction d''erreurs"],"de":["Neuschreibung von RuboCop in Rust","Verbesserung der Effizienz und Leistung","Open-Source-Code und anpassbar","Kompatibilität mit Ruby und Rust","Code-Analyse und Fehlerkorrektur"],"pt":["Reescrita experimental do RuboCop em Rust","Melhoria da performance e produtividade do desenvolvedor Ruby","Integração com o ecossistema Ruby","Suporte a funcionalidades avançadas do Rust","Código aberto e personalizável"],"ru":["Экспериментальная переписка RuboCop на Rust","Улучшение производительности и продуктивности разработчика Ruby","Интеграция с экосистемой Ruby","Поддержка расширенных функций Rust","Открытый и настраиваемый код"],"ar":["إعادة كتابة تجريبية لروبوكوب في روست","تحسين الأداء وإنتاجية مطور روبي","التكامل مع نظام روبي","دعم الميزات المتقدمة في روست","البرمجيات مفتوحة المصدر وقابلة للتعديل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用fix-repo","什么是RuboCop","fix-repo安装教程","Ruby代码质量优化","fix-repo vs RuboCop","Rust开发工具","代码静态分析工具","性能优化工具"],"ja":["fix-repoの使い方","RuboCopとは","fix-repoのインストール方法","Rubyコードの品質向上","fix-repo vs RuboCop","Rust開発ツール","コード静的解析ツール","パフォーマンス最適化ツール"],"ko":["fix-repo 사용법","루비코프란","fix-repo 설치 가이드","루비 코드 품질 최적화","fix-repo vs 루비코프","러스트 개발 도구","코드 정적 분석 도구","성능 최적화 도구"],"es":["herramientas de AI","fix-repo","RuboCop","Rust","Ruby","cómo usar fix-repo","alternativas a RuboCop","fix-repo vs RuboCop","instalación de fix-repo","guía de configuración de fix-repo"],"fr":["outils d''IA","fix-repo","RuboCop","Rust","Ruby","comment utiliser fix-repo","alternatives à RuboCop","fix-repo vs RuboCop","installation de fix-repo","guide de configuration de fix-repo"],"de":["KI-Tools","fix-repo","RuboCop","Rust","Ruby","wie man fix-repo verwendet","Alternativen zu RuboCop","fix-repo vs RuboCop","Installation von fix-repo","Konfigurationsanleitung für fix-repo"],"pt":["como usar Fix-Repo","o que é Fix-Repo","alternativas ao RuboCop","Fix-Repo vs RuboCop","instalar Fix-Repo","guia de configuração do Fix-Repo","desenvolvimento de software em Ruby","ferramentas de desenvolvimento em Rust"],"ru":["как использовать Fix-Repo","что такое Fix-Repo","альтернативы RuboCop","Fix-Repo vs RuboCop","установка Fix-Repo","руководство по настройке Fix-Repo","разработка программного обеспечения на Ruby","инструменты разработки на Rust"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أداة إصلاح المستودع","ما هي أداة إصلاح المستودع","بديلات روبوكوب","أداة إصلاح المستودع مقابل روبوكوب","تثبيت أداة إصلاح المستودع","دليل إعداد أداة إصلاح المستودع","تطوير البرمجيات باستخدام روبي","أدوات تطوير البرمجيات باستخدام روست"]}},"owner":"6","repo":"nitrocop","repoPath":"6/nitrocop","stars":1,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T21:47:43Z","topics":["rubocop","ruby","rust"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fix-repo","description":"Improve a specific repos corpus conformance by fixing its top diverging cops in parallel using worktree-isolated teammates.","bodyPreview":"# Fix Repo — Repo-Targeted Conformance Improvement\n\nThis skill targets a specific corpus repo (e.g., rails, discourse, mastodon) and fixes\nthe cops that contribute the most FP/FN for that repo. Unlike `/fix-cops` (globally worst\ncops) or `/fix-department` (all cops in a gem), this focuses on improving a specific repo''s\nmatch rate.\n\nIf you edit code yourself (without dispatching teammates), do that work in a dedicated\ngit worktree by default. Only skip this when the user explicitly asks to use th","body":"# Fix Repo — Repo-Targeted Conformance Improvement\n\nThis skill targets a specific corpus repo (e.g., rails, discourse, mastodon) and fixes\nthe cops that contribute the most FP/FN for that repo. Unlike `/fix-cops` (globally worst\ncops) or `/fix-department` (all cops in a gem), this focuses on improving a specific repo''s\nmatch rate.\n\nIf you edit code yourself (without dispatching teammates), do that work in a dedicated\ngit worktree by default. Only skip this when the user explicitly asks to use the current tree.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Phase 0: Assess (you do this)\n\n1. **If no repo was specified**, show the repo list and let the user pick:\n   ```bash\n   python3 scripts/investigate-repo.py --list $ARGUMENTS\n   ```\n\n2. **Once a repo is chosen**, run the repo investigation and **paste its full output\n   verbatim to the user** (the table IS the primary output — do not summarize or skip it):\n   ```bash\n   python3 scripts/investigate-repo.py <repo-name> $ARGUMENTS\n   ```\n   The script automatically excludes cops fixed since the last corpus oracle run\n   by scanning git commit messages, so the output only shows cops that still need work.\n\n3. Show the user the top diverging cops and confirm the target repo.\n\n### Phase 1: Full Table & Recommendations (you do this)\n\n1. **Show the complete table** of ALL diverging cops (use `--limit 0`) ordered by FP+FN\n   descending. This is the full picture of what needs to happen to reach 100%:\n   ```bash\n   python3 scripts/investigate-repo.py <repo-name> --limit 0 $ARGUMENTS\n   ```\n   Paste the full output verbatim to the user.\n\n2. **Check global FP/FN** for the top candidates (use `--repos-only | head -5` for each).\n   This helps prioritize cops where the target repo is a significant contributor.\n\n3. **Recommend up to 4 cops** to fix in this batch. Prioritize by impact (highest FP+FN\n   first), but use judgment about difficulty. Present your recommendations with global\n   context:\n   ```\n   My recommendations for this batch (4 cops):\n   1. Style/OptionHash — 91 FP on rails (1,819 FP globally), likely <hypothesis>\n   2. Layout/IndentationWidth — 0 FP, 5,696 FN on rails (Xk FN globally), likely <hypothesis>\n   3. ...\n\n   Want me to proceed with these, or would you like to swap any out?\n   ```\n\n   Don''t skip any cop category — Layout alignment cops, low-match-rate cops, and FN-heavy\n   cops are all fair game. The goal is 100% conformance, so everything needs to be tackled\n   eventually.\n\n**Wait for user confirmation before proceeding.** The user may want to pick different cops\nor adjust the batch size.\n\nOnce confirmed, investigate each selected cop''s FP/FN pattern in depth:\n```bash\npython3 scripts/investigate-cop.py Department/CopName --context --fp-only --limit 10\npython3 scripts/investigate-cop.py Department/CopName --context --fn-only --limit 10\n```\n\n**Run the delta reducer** on up to 3 examples per cop (mix of FP and FN) to get minimal reproductions:\n```bash\npython3 scripts/reduce-mismatch.py Department/CopName repo_id filepath:line            # FP\npython3 scripts/reduce-mismatch.py Department/CopName repo_id filepath:line --type fn   # FN\n```\nPick examples from different repos when possible. The reduced files (typically 5–20 lines) go\nto `/tmp/nitrocop-reduce/` — read them and include them in the teammate prompt.\n\nSummarize: cop name, repo-specific FP/FN, global FP/FN, minimal repro(s), root cause hypothesis.\n\n### Phase 2: Dispatch (you do this)\n\n1. Create a team:\n   ```\n   TeamCreate(team_name=\"fix-repo\", description=\"Improve <repo-name> conformance\")\n   ```\n\n2. Create tasks for each cop fix.\n\n3. Spawn one teammate per cop using the Task tool. **Critical settings:**\n   - `isolation: \"worktree\"` — each teammate gets its own git worktree\n   - `subagent_type: \"general-purpose\"` — needs full edit/bash access\n   - `team_name: \"fix-repo\"`\n   - `mode: \"bypassPermissions\"` — teammates need to run cargo test etc.\n\n4. Each teammate prompt MUST include:\n   - The exact cop name (e.g., `Lint/ConstantResolution`)\n   - The FP/FN counts (both repo-specific and global) and root cause hypothesis\n   - **The minimal repro(s) from the delta reducer** — paste the reduced Ruby source directly\n   - Whether to focus on FP fixes, FN fixes, or both\n   - A reminder that parallel-agent activity often leaves unrelated local modifications; those files are off-limits\n   - The teammate workflow (Phase 3 below) — paste the full instructions\n\n### Phase 3: Teammate Workflow (paste this into each teammate''s prompt)\n\n```\nYou are fixing false positives/negatives in a single nitrocop cop to improve corpus\nconformance for a target repo. Follow the CLAUDE.md rules strictly.\n\n**NEVER use git stash or git stash pop.** You are in an isolated git worktree — just commit directly.\nParallel-agent activity is common. If you see unrelated modified files, do not edit/revert them.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Read the cop source** at `src/cop/<dept>/<cop_name>.rs`\n   Read the vendor RuboCop spec at `vendor/rubocop*/spec/rubocop/cop/<dept>/<cop_name>_spec.rb`\n   **Check for existing investigation comments** (marked with \"Known false positives\" or\n   \"reverted\") — these document previously attempted fixes that regressed on corpus\n   validation. Do NOT repeat the same approach. Either find a different root cause or\n   extend the prior approach to avoid its documented failure mode.\n\n2. **Understand the FP/FN pattern** from the examples provided in your prompt.\n   If needed, read the actual source files from `vendor/corpus/<repo_id>/<path>` to see more context.\n\n3. **Add test cases (TDD)**:\n   - For FP fixes: add the false-positive pattern to `tests/fixtures/cops/<dept>/<cop_name>/no_offense.rb`\n   - For FN fixes: add the missed detection to `tests/fixtures/cops/<dept>/<cop_name>/offense.rb`\n   - Run `cargo test --release -p nitrocop --lib -- <cop_name_snake>` to verify the test FAILS\n\n4. **Fix the cop implementation** in `src/cop/<dept>/<cop_name>.rs`\n\n5. **Verify**:\n   - `cargo test --release -p nitrocop --lib -- <cop_name_snake>` — all tests pass\n   - `cargo fmt`\n   - `cargo clippy --release -- -D warnings`\n\n6. **Commit your fix**:\n   ```bash\n   git add src/cop/<dept>/<cop_name>.rs tests/fixtures/cops/<dept>/<cop_name>/\n   # Add any other changed files\n   git commit -m \"Fix <Department/CopName> false positives/negatives\n\n   <one-line description of what was wrong>\n\n   Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n   ```\n   Stage only files for this cop fix. Do not include unrelated modified files.\n\n7. **Report back** via SendMessage with:\n   - What the root cause was\n   - What you changed\n   - Whether tests pass\n   - The commit SHA\n   - If you could NOT fix it: explain why and whether it should be deferred\n```\n\n### Phase 4: Collect Results (you do this)\n\n1. Wait for all teammates to report back.\n\n2. For each completed fix:\n   - Note the worktree branch name from the Task result\n   - Cherry-pick or merge the commit into your working branch\n\n3. Run full verification:\n   ```bash\n   cargo fmt\n   cargo clippy --release -- -D warnings\n   cargo test --release\n   ```\n\n4. Verify each fixed cop against the corpus:\n   ```bash\n   python3 scripts/check-cop.py Department/CopName --verbose --rerun\n   ```\n   **Corpus validation is the acceptance gate** — unit tests passing is necessary but\n   NOT sufficient.\n\n5. **Handle regressions**: if a fix increases FP count (even if unit tests pass), revert\n   the code change but **add a detailed investigation comment** to the cop source file\n   documenting what was tried, why it regressed, and what a correct fix would need. Use:\n   ```rust\n   /// ## Known false positives (N FP in corpus as of YYYY-MM-DD)\n   ///\n   /// An attempt was made to ... (commit XXXXXXXX, reverted). The approach: ...\n   /// This fixed the target FPs but introduced N NEW false positives (X→Y FP).\n   /// Root cause of regression: ...\n   /// A correct fix needs to: ...\n   ```\n\n6. Re-run the repo investigation to show updated status:\n   ```bash\n   python3 scripts/investigate-repo.py <repo-name>\n   ```\n   Note: This still reads the original corpus data. Per-cop verification via check-cop.py\n   gives the ground truth for fixed cops.\n\n6. Report to the user:\n   - Which cops were fixed (with FP/FN counts)\n   - Estimated impact on the target repo''s match rate\n   - Which cops couldn''t be fixed (and why)\n   - Summary of changes ready for commit/PR\n\n## Arguments\n\n- `/fix-repo` — show repo list, let user pick\n- `/fix-repo rails` — fix top diverging cops for the rails repo\n- `/fix-repo discourse` — fix top diverging cops for discourse\n- `/fix-repo rails --fp-only` — only fix FP-producing cops for rails\n- `/fix-repo --input /path/to/corpus-results.json rails` — use local corpus file\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:06:17.775Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing targeted repository conformance improvement with RuboCop and Rust","zh":"适合需要针对特定仓库使用 RuboCop 和 Rust 进行代码分析并改进一致性的代码分析代理","ja":"RuboCop と Rust を使用して特定のリポジトリのコード分析と一貫性の改善が必要なコード分析エージェントに適しています","ko":"RuboCop와 Rust를 사용하여 특정 저장소의 코드 분석 및 일관성 개선을 필요로 하는 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de código que necesitan mejorar la conformidad del repositorio objetivo con RuboCop y Rust","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant une amélioration ciblée de la conformité du référentiel avec RuboCop et Rust","de":"Perfekt für Code-Analyse-Agents, die eine gezielte Verbesserung der Repository-Konformität mit RuboCop und Rust benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Código que precisam de melhoria de conformidade de repositório direcionada com RuboCop e Rust","ru":"Идеально для Агентов Анализа Кодов, которым необходима целенаправленная оптимизация соответствия репозитория с помощью RuboCop и Rust","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى تحسين التماثل المستهدف ل仓 مخزن باستخدام RuboCop و Rust"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to improve a specific corpus repo''s match rate by fixing cops that contribute the most false positives/false negatives, utilizing a dedicated git worktree for seamless code editing and leveraging Experimental RuboCop rewrite in Rust for enhanced performance","zh":"赋予代理改进特定代码库的匹配率的能力，通过修复导致最多假阳性/假阴性的 cop，并利用专用的 git worktree 进行无缝的代码编辑，并利用实验性的 RuboCop 重写以提高性能","ja":"特定コーパスリポジトリのマッチ率を改善するために、最も多くの偽陽性/偽陰性を引き起こす cop を修正し、シームレスなコード編集のための専用の git worktree を利用し、パフォーマンスを向上させるために Rust で実験的に書き直された RuboCop を利用するエージェントを可能にします","ko":"특정 코퍼스 저장소의 일치율을 개선할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하여 가장 많은 거짓 양성/거짓 음성을 유발하는 cop를 수정하고, 코드 편집을 위한 전용 git worktree를 활용하며, 성능을 향상시키기 위해 Rust에서 실험적으로 다시 작성된 RuboCop를 활용합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mejorar la tasa de coincidencia de un repositorio de corpus específico al corregir los cops que contribuyen con los falsos positivos/negativos más significativos, utilizando un git worktree dedicado para una edición de código sin problemas y aprovechando la reescritura experimental de RuboCop en Rust para un mejor rendimiento","fr":"Permet aux agents d''améliorer le taux de correspondance d''un référentiel de corpus spécifique en corrigeant les cops qui contribuent le plus aux faux positifs/négatifs, en utilisant un git worktree dédié pour une édition de code sans problème et en exploitant la réécriture expérimentale de RuboCop en Rust pour des performances améliorées","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, die Übereinstimmungsrate eines bestimmten Corpus-Repositorys zu verbessern, indem sie die cops korrigieren, die die meisten falschen Positiven/Negativen beitragen, unter Verwendung eines dedizierten git worktree für eine nahtlose Codebearbeitung und unter Ausnutzung des experimentellen RuboCop-Neuschreibens in Rust für eine verbesserte Leistung","pt":"Habilita agentes a melhorar a taxa de correspondência de um repositório de corpus específico, corrigindo cops que contribuem para os falsos positivos/negativos, utilizando uma árvore de trabalho git dedicada para edição de código sem interrupções e aproveitando a reescrita experimental do RuboCop em Rust para desempenho aprimorado","ru":"Позволяет агентам улучшить коэффициент соответствия конкретного репозитория корпуса, исправляя cops, которые способствуют возникновению ложных положительных/отрицательных результатов, используя выделенную рабочую область git для бесшовного редактирования кода и используя экспериментальную переписку RuboCop на Rust для повышения производительности","ar":"تمكين العميل من تحسين معدل المطابقة لمستودع корпус معين من خلال إصلاح الشرطة التي تساهم في الإيجابيات/Khlt السلبية الخاطئة، باستخدام شجرة عمل جيت مخصصة لتحرير الشفرة بسلاسة واستخدام إعادة كتابة RuboCop التجريبية في Rust لتحسين الأداء"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code conformance improvement for specific repositories like rails, discourse, or mastodon","Debugging repository-specific cops to reduce false positives/false negatives","Enhancing repository match rates with targeted cop fixes"],"zh":["自动化特定仓库（如 rails、discourse 或 mastodon）的代码一致性改进","调试仓库特定的 cop 以减少假阳性/假阴性","通过有针对性的 cop 修复来增强仓库的匹配率"],"ja":["rails、discourse、または mastodon などの特定のリポジトリのコード一貫性の改善の自動化","偽陽性/偽陰性を減らすためにリポジトリ固有の cop のデバッグ","ターゲットを絞った cop の修正によるリポジトリのマッチ率の向上"],"ko":["특정 저장소(rails, discourse 또는 mastodon 등)의 코드 일관성 개선을 자동화하는 것","거짓 양성/거짓 음성을 줄이기 위해 저장소 특정 cop를 디버깅하는 것","저장소의 일치율을 향상시키기 위해 대상이 되는 cop를 수정하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar la mejora de la conformidad del código para repositorios específicos como rails, discourse o mastodon","Depurar cops de repositorio específicos para reducir los falsos positivos/negativos","Mejorar las tasas de coincidencia del repositorio con correcciones de cop dirigidas"],"fr":["Automatiser l''amélioration de la conformité du code pour des référentiels spécifiques comme rails, discourse ou mastodon","Déboguer les cops de référentiel spécifiques pour réduire les faux positifs/négatifs","Améliorer les taux de correspondance du référentiel avec des corrections de cop ciblées"],"de":["Automatisieren der Verbesserung der Code-Konformität für bestimmte Repositorys wie rails, discourse oder mastodon","Debuggen von Repository-spezifischen cops, um falsche Positiven/Negativen zu reduzieren","Verbessern der Repository-Übereinstimmungsraten mit gezielten cop-Korrekturen"],"pt":["Automatizar a melhoria da conformidade de código para repositórios específicos, como rails, discourse ou mastodon","Depurar cops específicos de repositório para reduzir falsos positivos/negativos","Aumentar as taxas de correspondência de repositório com consertos de cops direcionados"],"ru":["Автоматизировать улучшение соответствия кода для конкретных репозиториев, таких как rails, discourse или mastodon","Отладить cops, специфичных для репозитория, чтобы уменьшить количество ложных положительных/отрицательных результатов","Повысить коэффициент соответствия репозитория с помощью целенаправленных исправлений cops"],"ar":["أتمتة تحسين التماثل الشفرة لمستودعات معينة مثل rails و discourse و mastodon","تصحيح الأخطاء في الشرطة الخاصة بمستودع لخفض الإيجابيات/Khlt السلبية الخاطئة","تحسين معدل المطابقة لمستودع مع تحسينات الشرطة المستهدفة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires repository access and write permissions","Limited to repositories with RuboCop integration","Default usage requires a dedicated git worktree"],"zh":["需要仓库访问和写入权限","仅限于具有 RuboCop 集成的仓库","默认使用需要专用的 git worktree"],"ja":["リポジトリへのアクセスと書き込み権限が必要","RuboCop 統合を持つリポジトリのみに対応","デフォルトの使用では専用の git worktree が必要"],"ko":["저장소에 대한 액세스 및 쓰기 권한이 필요합니다","RuboCop 통합을 가진 저장소에만 제한됩니다","기본 사용에는 전용 git worktree가 필요합니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso al repositorio y permisos de escritura","Limitado a repositorios con integración de RuboCop","Uso predeterminado requiere un git worktree dedicado"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au référentiel et des autorisations d''écriture","Limité aux référentiels avec intégration de RuboCop","Utilisation par défaut nécessite un git worktree dédié"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf das Repository und Schreibberechtigungen","Begrenzt auf Repositorys mit RuboCop-Integration","Standardmäßige Verwendung erfordert ein dediziertes git worktree"],"pt":["Requer acesso e permissões de gravação ao repositório","Limitado a repositórios com integração do RuboCop","Uso padrão requer uma árvore de trabalho git dedicada"],"ru":["Требует доступа и разрешений на запись в репозиторий","Ограничен репозиториями с интеграцией RuboCop","Стандартное использование требует выделенной рабочей области git"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول والسماحيات الكتابة إلى المستودع","محدود بالمستودعات التي لديها دمج RuboCop","الاستخدام الافتراضي يتطلب شجرة عمل جيت مخصصة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"eec6bd903653d532718c685bb17e671550ddcba06d8c24dfce6253c3bd68858b","qualityScore":52}');
